      "data": {
        "tag": "Spelling",
        "ruleName": "Accent on every question word",
        "anchor": "A question word always carries a written accent: qué, quién, dónde, cuándo, cómo, cuánto.",
        "prerequisites": [
          "Without the accent the word has another job: que (that), como (like, as), cuando (when, in a statement).",
          "The question opens with ¿ and closes with ?.",
          "The accent does not change the sound of the letters; it tells the reader \"this is a question word\"."
        ]
